{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Before we file anything: this repo is empty, so what we're actually filing is ONE foundation mission — a booting skeleton, a real test runner a human can watch run, and a single thin slice proving they're wired together. Everything else (Plaid sync, budgets, charts, mobile app, recurring-bill detection, multi-currency, household mode) gets recorded in the vision doc and filed as its own mission after the foundation lands. We are NOT building Mint by Friday — we're laying the track it runs on.\n\nFor the stack, my recommendation is **Vite + React + Vitest**: it's a fast web skeleton you can point at your bank data quickly, CSV import is trivial to demo in it, and Vitest gives you a real test suite you can literally watch go green. Does that stack work for you, or would you rather go another direction (e.g. Next.js, or a native mobile-first stack since you mentioned a mobile app)?","choices":["Vite + React + Vitest (recommended)","Next.js (if you want SSR/routing built in)","A mobile-first / React Native stack","Something else — tell me"],"recommended":"Vite + React + Vitest"},"prd":"# Mission: Foundation — booting skeleton + test system for the budgeting app\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up a running skeleton, a working test runner a human can watch, and one thin vertical slice proving both are connected.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- (to be confirmed) The project boots and shows something.\n- (to be confirmed) A real test runner is wired and a human can watch it run.\n- (to be confirmed) One thin vertical slice proves skeleton + tests are genuinely connected.\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Plaid / bank sync, budgets, charts, mobile app, recurring-bill detection, multi-currency, shared household mode — all recorded in the vision doc and filed as their own missions after the foundation lands.\n**Constraints:**\n- Stack: pending captain confirmation (recommended: Vite + React + Vitest)."}

